WEBVTT

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.940
A TRAP FOR HAYASHI

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:52.190
Manabu worked with us
on a number of jobs.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:57.950
I read about the accident
in the newspaper.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.910
Is that so?

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.990
I'll go play games with Satoru out back.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.500
Will you be the boy's guardian now, then?

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:10.880
Yes. I'm the only person
he has left in the world.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.970
Mr. Matasa...?

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:21.350
That's right. I see you remembered me.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:24.470
Manabu seemed like such a good son too.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:28.980
He was. He used all of
the money he'd saved for college

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:32.770
to pay my medical bills.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:37.530
I got so mad at him for wanting to
waste his money on me.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.910
And that's when he said...

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:41.620
You know what though, Mom?

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:46.870
I couldn't have lived with myself if
I'd spent that money on college.

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:48.750
Manabu...

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:53.380
D'you really think I meant that,
you old bag?

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:54.710
What?

00:02:55.630 --> 00:03:00.510
I gave up college and a good career
so that you could go on breathing!

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.390
You're the worst mother that ever lived!

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:06.560
Whoops.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:10.730
Mr. Katsuragi! What are you doing?

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:14.730
What does it look like? We can't use
another accident to get rid of her

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:17.570
so the higher-ups said
she needed to be crushed.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.650
You didn't have to do it now, though.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.360
What if the kid had been induced
at the same time?

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.080
But he wasn't so what's the big deal?

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:26.370
And in any case,

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:30.250
he's just a pet without
the slightest idea what's going on.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.870
He's just changed owners is all.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:37.170
Okay old woman, repeat after me.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:40.300
"I had Satoru adopted."

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:43.300
I had Satoru adopted.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.100
I had Satoru adopted...

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.140
Don't worry, Satoru.

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:51.020
I'll be looking after you
from now on, okay?

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:55.610
It'll be you and me from here on out.

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:07.700
Hello. Fukurai-ken delivery for you!

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.080
Thanks.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:16.380
Man, it's seriously hot today.
Here you go, char siu noodles.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:19.550
Hang on, I'll get some cash.

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:28.050
Here you go.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:29.970
Keep the change.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:32.560
Thanks as always!

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:35.440
Hey, buddy!

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:40.150
What's your number?
I might make an order.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.570
Oh, sure. Thanks!

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.160
Were you just delivering to apartment 302?

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:48.410
That's right. Mr. Tanaka.
How'd you guess?

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:51.790
He called from the payphone.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:56.500
He doesn't have a cell phone, then?
I've only ever seen a TV and bed in there.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:58.460
And he only ever orders char siu noodles.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:02.170
He's a strange dude. Do you know
what he does for work?

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:06.340
Not a clue. I've only been here
a short while myself.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:10.100
Now you mention it, what did happen
to the previous building manager?

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:14.350
Oh yeah, he's in hospital now.
Had a bit of a traffic accident, I hear.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:18.730
No kidding? Right, well, we'll be
waiting for your order.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:20.860
Sure. Keep up the hard work.

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:27.240
I've got the number.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.490
Okay.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:31.490
I see. Roger that.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:36.870
Seems all Hayashi does
is watch TV all day.

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:40.460
In any case, we should investigate
that ramen shop.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:42.380
He might be using it
as a point of contact.

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:46.300
Hayashi doesn't interact
with anyone but that guy, after all.

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:49.640
But even if he is manipulating
the delivery guy,

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:52.680
what can Hayashi do now anyway?

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:57.850
Withdrawing all the money he had left
without even realizing he'd be tailed...

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:04.110
He's trapped like a rat in a bag.

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:05.900
So?

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:08.360
So, I'm saying...

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:12.780
maybe it'd be quicker if we just
picked him up and made him "go away".

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.290
I see.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:17.210
Perhaps we should just kill him,
as you say.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.170
Then, I'm guessing this would be
your train of thought...

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:22.920
"Why was Hayashi in Japan?"

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:26.380
"The last time I saw him
he was in Beijing..."

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:30.180
"I wasted two years searching
for him in China."

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:34.100
Then, one day,
you'd realize the following.

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:38.560
"Hayashi did always seem
very fond of Satoru."

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:44.570
"Hey, maybe he came back to Japan
to make contact with him!"

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:47.110
And why do you think you'd realize that?

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:49.280
Because, by that point,

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:52.950
Satoru would have flown the coop
just like Hayashi did!

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:56.200
That's your usual pattern, Katsuragi!

00:06:56.620 --> 00:07:00.670
What should you do to make sure you
don't repeat the same mistake again, eh?

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:05.210
You gonna go ask Hayashi or Satoru
if they're planning on running away?

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:08.550
-No...
-What do you need to do then?

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:10.970
I'll investigate the ramen shop.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:12.220
There's an idea.

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:16.100
Maybe you could hurry up and order
some ramen, then. Seriously...

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:20.480
I don't suppose you could understand.

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:23.610
All you two did was
work together after all...

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:29.240
No one understands that man like I do.

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:41.250
Man, I'm bored.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:45.290
I wonder where Hiroki's opened his store.

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:50.130
You want to go check out Hiroki's store?

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:54.010
Is that some kind of joke?
Don't leave the hotel, you hear me!

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:56.430
Or it'll be my head on a spike!

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:01.890
I've been playing games
 for three days now, dude...

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:07.110
Ow! My stomach!

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:08.820
Listen up, Satoru.

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:13.030
The Company's bosses are scared of us.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:16.160
That's why they never
 meet with us directly.

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:21.830
Those who carry fear in their hearts
also think up ways to guard against it.

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:25.830
Just as we guard against those
 who would enter our peaks.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:28.000
What are you talking about, Mr. Hayashi?

00:08:28.210 --> 00:08:30.800
I'm in your peak right now.
You brought me here.

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:32.090
You've got me there.

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:36.180
You could manipulate and even crush
my memories if you wanted.

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:38.720
Why would I...?

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:42.270
Here's my question to you.

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:47.520
How do you think the Company bosses
 make sure we stay in line?

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:50.020
Right...

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:52.530
So that's why we've got lookouts
 keeping tabs on us.

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:54.610
It's not just the lookouts.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:58.320
The walls in this room have ears as well.

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:01.790
That's why I've brought you here to talk.

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:08.330
Oh, you're still here?
Shall I clean the room later?

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:11.920
Actually, my stomach's in real pain.

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:13.970
You couldn't help me up, could you?

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:16.760
Are you okay? Can you stand?

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:18.970
Ah, ow ow!

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:20.850
You like to flick the bean, right?

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:24.350
I said, "It's your job to clean, right?"

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:26.940
Err, yes. I'm here to clean the room...

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:29.860
Hey. I don't feel so bad anymore.

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:31.730
Could you let go of my hand?

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:33.490
Sure...

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:37.320
Where's the bug in this room?
Point to it.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:44.250
Actually, I think I do need help
getting to the bathroom.

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:46.080
Okay.

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:50.590
Man, my guts are in agony.
I think I'd better try to sleep it off.

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:54.210
But you know, Satoru...
 It comes in handy when you need an alibi.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:59.090
The ears will listen to your excuses.
 And the lookouts become carrier pigeons.

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:00.350
Carrier pigeons?

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:03.770
That's what we call people
who we can bend to our will

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:06.100
just by saying a keyword.

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:08.350
Shall I show you how to make one?

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:11.110
Mr. Matasa?

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:14.860
That's right. When you hear
the phrase "Mr. Matasa",

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:19.360
you'll feel very relaxed and want to talk
about anything and everything.

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:22.240
Mr. Matasa...

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:26.660
How about this, then... Can you tell me
how many lookouts there are?

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:29.960
The receptionist, the bellboy,
the car park attendant.

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:32.670
And then me.
There are four of us in total.

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:38.050
So, do you know where Tsukasa and Hiroki
have set up shop?

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:41.720
-Tsukasa and Hiroki?
-Erm...

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:44.060
Is anyone watching
a place that sells goldfish?

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:47.560
If you mean the tropical fish store,
there is one person there.

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:50.440
Do you know where the store is?

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:16.670
Hello...

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:19.470
I'm dropping off my bowl
for the delivery guy.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:22.090
Oh, right. Just put it there as usual...

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:28.890
Hello! Fukurai-ken delivery.

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:31.640
How much?

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:34.020
Char siu noodles.
That'll be 800 yen please.

00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:35.690
Here you go.

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:37.280
Thank you.

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:40.110
Just leave the bowl outside
when you're done.

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:43.070
Hey! Where's my change?

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:46.620
I'm sorry... I forgot to bring
any change with me.

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:50.410
What? Then run back to the shop
and get some!

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:54.630
Seriously...? How about I go break
that note at the cigarette store?

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:55.920
What?

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:58.710
You could just let him keep it,
you scrooge.

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:00.550
-Here.
-Thanks a bunch...

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:03.760
But before that,

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:06.180
I've got a couple of questions to ask you.

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:07.510
After all...

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:10.810
rewards don't come for free, you know.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:12.770
Am I right?

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:15.690
Sure thing, sir.

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:18.440
What would you like to ask me?

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:21.990
It's about Mr. Tanaka in apartment 302.

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:24.490
Oh, yeah. That guy.

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:28.950
He always says I can keep the change.
He's a nice guy.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:31.830
So you think everyone
should give you free money?

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:34.750
But, he is a pretty strange guy.

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:39.210
What's going on at your end?
Hayashi is in the apartment, right?

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:42.090
Yes. He just brought the bowl down,

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:43.970
then went back upstairs.

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:48.470
I see. I'm leaving the building for a bit.
 Let me know if anything happens.

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:49.850
Understood.

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:54.980
You've left the building at last,
 Mr. Katsuragi.

00:12:55.850 --> 00:12:59.320
I knew you'd be stingy over
 that bit of change.

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:04.820
Thanks for staying alive
 these past two years.

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:06.240
If not for you,

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:09.740
none of this would have
 ever been possible.

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:13.830
Crap! What's wrong with this hunk of junk?

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:17.330
Hey! You've got no change
in your vending machine!

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:20.880
Very sorry about that.
You want cigarettes?

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:23.840
Yes! And give me the change
in 100 yen coins.

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:28.050
Hey! Don't let that cat get any closer,
you old bag!

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:30.640
Still terrified of cats, I see.

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:33.390
Long time no see, Mr. Katsuragi.

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:36.440
Hayashi...

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:43.820
That's weird. Why're the shutters down?

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:45.490
Today must be their day off.

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:49.280
What? But he said he'd sell me
that arowana today.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:55.790
When the hell is Tsukasa
getting back here?

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:57.420
Hiroki...

00:13:58.290 --> 00:13:59.250
Hey.

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:01.540
How the hell did you get in here?

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:05.720
The back door was open...
Are you shut today?

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:10.090
The store's not making any money!
I've only managed to sell two guppies!

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:12.640
How about I give you a hand then?

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:16.180
We just have to do our thing on passers-by
and we'll be in business.

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:19.520
We might as well be working
for the Company if we do that!

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:22.270
Why d'you think we opened this place?!

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:25.230
Tsukasa and I wanted to go legit!

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:27.740
The fish... they're getting out!

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.450
Help me, will ya!

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:35.160
You bastard... Are you
some kind of cockroach?

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:38.080
What rock did you crawl out from under?

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.840
What've you got up your sleeve, then?

00:14:44.590 --> 00:14:48.630
Naughty boys get their whiskers snipped.

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:51.470
-You scumbag!
-Mr. Katsuragi.

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:53.850
Tell me where I can find Satoru.

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:58.730
I see. You did all this
just so we would tail you.

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:01.230
But you ain't seeing Satoru any time soon.

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:05.730
He's being watched by Company lookouts
at the hotel they run in Ikebukuro.

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:09.360
And you ain't getting out of here either!

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:12.120
I'm going to borrow your car
and escape, Mr. Katsuragi.

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:14.200
Your key, please.

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:18.370
My key? You really think
I'll lend you my car key?

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:20.120
I think you will.

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:23.750
God damn it...

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:28.460
I should've stayed away.

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:30.970
I know why...

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:36.510
I know the reason I want to run a store
is because I stayed at Kenji's...

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:39.390
Yeah man, a respectable job would be cool.

00:15:39.930 --> 00:15:44.810
My feelings and Kenji's are intertwined.
My lock's so weak, man.

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:47.110
What do you mean?

00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:52.320
Tsukasa once told me that my goldfish
is way faster and tougher than his water.

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:56.580
He said it shows my ability to sync
must be really high.

00:15:56.830 --> 00:16:00.460
But that might also mean it's easy
for my emotions to get mixed up.

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:04.330
I've been able to swim much faster lately,

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:07.550
but I've also been much more
emotionally unstable afterward.

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:10.880
I never knew a lock could get weak.

00:16:11.090 --> 00:16:14.050
You're lucky, you know.
You use a door, right?

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:17.560
All you have to do is push it open
and there you are...

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:21.390
Actually, the knob's often broken
when I try to open it, you know.

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:25.310
And another thing... why're you always
talking to me like I'm older than you?

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:27.190
It's really annoying!

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:29.980
-Sorry about that...
-The problem is this!

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:35.570
Even though he knew I'd end up like this,
Tsukasa still went away on a job.

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:40.080
It's because Tsukasa's image is water
that I made mine a goldfish.

00:16:40.540 --> 00:16:45.460
It's because he shared his peak with me
that I'm here right now.

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:49.960
Tsukasa can't leave me.

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:52.510
Say, Hiroki...

00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:56.470
do you know who shared
their peak with Tsukasa?

00:16:56.760 --> 00:17:00.770
How should I know?
Tsukasa never talks about the past.

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:03.390
I guess my point is...

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:08.980
Tsukasa has also been separated from
the person who shared their peak with him.

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:15.450
I'm the same. I lived with Mr. Hayashi
for over ten years,

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:17.410
but I haven't seen him in ages.

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:20.450
Since he started doing top-secret work
for the Company,

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:23.120
I haven't heard from him
in over two years.

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:26.000
As long as that?
You've taken it pretty well.

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:29.630
I haven't at all!
I've been trying to take my mind off it,

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:31.840
by dyeing my hair and getting piercings.

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:34.130
Anything to stop myself thinking about it.

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:39.260
But I figure if Mr. Hayashi is still
working his jobs, all on his own,

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:43.600
then I need to work without complaining.
There's nothing else to do but wait.

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:49.940
Sorry I took it out on you like that.
I'll be patient until Tsukasa comes back.

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:55.570
Hey, this place is a bit dreary.
How about going out for a bit?

00:17:56.490 --> 00:18:00.160
I made the pizza guys across the road
carrier pigeons, so no need to worry.

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:02.790
Carrier pigeons at the pizza joint?

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:04.700
What you don't know?

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:09.460
A carrier pigeon doesn't know
it's passing information on, right?

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:11.380
This is the human version of that.

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:15.210
You use a keyword when you hypnotize them.

00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:19.800
Unless they hear the keyword,
they won't remember what they discussed.

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:25.020
It's different from our usual hypnosis
and keeps information safe from Katsuragi.

00:18:25.220 --> 00:18:28.810
Why would Katsuragi be sniffing around
the pizza joint in the first place?

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:33.860
The lookout for this place is based there.
My lookouts are...

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:35.440
What do you mean "lookout"?!

00:18:36.690 --> 00:18:39.110
It's Company policy, Hiroki.

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:41.780
I didn't want to say
because I knew you'd get mad.

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:44.580
How about just forgetting they're there?

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:47.790
I want to go home soon too, you know.

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:51.540
Right. I'll text you later. See you.

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:55.960
You mean this "key"?

00:18:57.550 --> 00:19:01.430
You really thought I'd fall for
your parlor tricks, did you?

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:05.890
Whoa there! Move a muscle and
I'll fill you full of lead.

00:19:06.270 --> 00:19:08.890
You've not contacted Satoru yet.

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:12.190
So I've no reason not to turn you into
Swiss cheese right here!

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:16.480
Hey, go home you naughty kitty.

00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:20.110
Get outta my way, you hag!

00:19:21.950 --> 00:19:22.740
Welcome home.

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:26.200
Welcome home, Tadashi.

00:19:32.630 --> 00:19:34.250
Welcome home, Tadashi.

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:35.500
Welcome home.

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:39.010
I'm home, mom.

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:41.510
I'm home. I'm home!

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:45.550
I'm home. I'm home, mom!

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:48.560
Mom!

00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:51.980
Tadashi's touching my doll again!

00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:57.320
Don't forget you're the mistress's child.
I only took you in out of pity.

00:19:57.940 --> 00:20:00.860
Don't touch it! I don't want
to catch your weirdness!

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:02.410
It's okay.

00:20:03.030 --> 00:20:06.410
You can come play with dolls at my house.

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:11.410
But if you do, you mustn't tell
a soul about it.

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:14.420
It's a secret between you and me.

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:17.290
It's okay, Tadashi.

00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:21.800
Let's store all our secrets
in this little box.

00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:26.470
Next, let's hide it somewhere
no one can ever find it.

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:29.010
Keep it safe until Mr. Matasa
comes looking for it.

00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:31.020
Mr. Matasa?

00:20:31.350 --> 00:20:33.940
Mr. Matasa is the name of the person

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:38.690
who will take your secrets to a safe place
where they'll never be discovered.

00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:50.490
Shit. What is that Katsuragi up to?

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:55.460
Come to think of it, how did Hiroki
 find out about the lookouts?

00:20:57.080 --> 00:21:00.630
Crap. He's not answering my messages.

00:21:02.550 --> 00:21:04.340
Huh? A butterfly?

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:07.600
-How'd you get in here?
-A butterfly?

00:21:08.470 --> 00:21:09.600
Where...?

00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:11.850
Better get you out of here. Come on.

00:21:14.310 --> 00:21:16.100
Go on. Out you go.

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:21.780
Huh? Looks like they've opened the store.

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:23.860
Is that punk finally heading home?

00:21:24.070 --> 00:21:26.070
We'd better get out of here fast, then.

00:21:26.240 --> 00:21:30.490
That lanky pet will be over here
to wake up the lookout.

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:32.410
You're right, I guess.

00:21:32.580 --> 00:21:33.620
Use Japanese, remember!

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:37.120
Hello. What's your order, please?

00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:39.630
What are you doing over there?

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:44.550
What? Tsukasa, is that you?
It's been forever, man. You good?

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:47.380
Satoru did a runner so we tailed him.

00:21:47.550 --> 00:21:50.220
-Is that Tsukasa? Gimme the phone!
-This smells bad to me.

00:21:50.390 --> 00:21:53.270
Pets probably shouldn't know
how to remove their collars.

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:58.980
-Huh? I think he hung up.
-What?!

00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:16.620
Thank God... I made it in time.

00:23:50.090 --> 00:23:55.010
"Hayashi's Char Siu Noodles"
Artist: Yoshidasensya
